nomos</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>27</volume><issue>6</issue><year>1995</year><fpage>906</fpage><lpage>912</lpage><article-title>Strength improvements with 1 yr of progressive resistance training in older women</article-title><source>Med Sci Sports Exerc</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7658954</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kraemer</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Adams</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Cafarelli</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Dudley</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Dooly</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Feigenbaum</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>34</volume><issue>2</issue><year>2002</year><fpage>364</fpage><lpage>380</lpage><article-title>American College of Sports Medicine position stand. Progression models in resistance training for healthy adults</article-title><source>Med Sci Sports Exerc</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11828249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pruitt</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Taaffe</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Marcus</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><volume>10</volume><issue>11</issue><year>1995</year><fpage>1788</fpage><lpage>1795</lpage><article-title>Effects of a one-year high-intensity versus low-intensity resistance training program on bone mineral density in older women</article-title><source>J Bone Miner Res</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8592957</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Clements</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fiatarone</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><volume>52</volume><issue>1</issue><year>1997</year><fpage>M27</fpage><lpage>M35</lpage><article-title>randomized controlled trial of progressive resistance training in depressed elders</article-title><source>J Gerontol A Biol Sci Med Sci</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9008666</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Fiatarone</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Morganti</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Trice</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Greenberg</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name></person-group><volume>272</volume><issue>24</issue><year>1994</year><fpage>1909</fpage><lpage>1914</lpage><article-title>Effects of high-intensity strength training on multiple risk factors for osteoporotic fractures. A randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>JAMA</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7990242</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Layne</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nuernberger</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Judge</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaliton</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><volume>29</volume><i